{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Base directory for this skill: /tmp/scratch/skillhost/.claude/skills/persona-judge\n\n# persona-judge\n\nEach persona is judged by what its text makes the agent do, not by what its author meant. The review runs in its own\nagent, the reviewer, so the session that asked for it neither shapes nor softens the score.\n\n## Files\n\n- [`reviewer.md`](reviewer.md): the reviewer's persona, with its rules and what it returns.\n- [`references/reviewing.md`](references/reviewing.md): the reviewer's steps; the reviewer loads it, and you do not.\n- [`references/review-questions.md`](references/review-questions.md): the questions, scales, weights and formula.\n- [`references/sample-review.md`](references/sample-review.md): the form every report takes.\n- [`references/persona-boundaries.md`](references/persona-boundaries.md): what a persona is and is not.\n- [`references/bibliography.md`](references/bibliography.md): the source behind each question, loaded only when\n  someone asks for one.\n- `scripts/`: the scripts that find the personas, run the checks and compute the score.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. **Check Python.** Run `python3 --version`. The scripts need Python 3.11 or later and nothing beyond its standard\n   library. When Python is missing or older, tell the user that and give no score, because the score comes only from\n   `scripts/report.py`.\n2. **Start the reviewer.** Start a subagent whose brief opens with the full text of [`reviewer.md`](reviewer.md) below\n   its front matter, then gives this folder's absolute path and what the user named: files, folders or pasted text.\n   With nothing named, it reviews the whole project.\n3. **Report a reviewer that cannot start.** When the reviewer cannot be started, tell the user that and why, and give\n   no score, because the review runs apart from your session and you do not run it yourself.\n4. **Pass on what it returns.** Give the user the reviewer's output as it is, the report or the reason there is none,\n   with nothing added, because anything you add would read as part of the review.\n\n## Mistakes to avoid\n\n- Answering the review questions yourself when the reviewer fails: return the failure instead, because a score from\n  your session carries your session's instructions into it.\n- Summarising the report, or leading with your own view of it: give it whole, because the quoted lines are what the\n  author acts on and a summary drops them.\n- Rewriting a line the report quotes, unasked: offer nothing, because *persona-judge* leaves every change and its\n  wording to the author.\n\n\nARGUMENTS: .github/agents/"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "a906745e-2514-460f-b0e1-81208c1b4eba", "uuid": "592f53c5-0e0a-4012-a5ec-fcd463a3505f", "timestamp": "2026-10-04T07:47:04.773Z", "isSynthetic": true}
